### Scanner access limit

A club can have a maximum of **four active Core Members with QR-scanning permission**.

This is a strict business rule.

The President and Vice President are separate leadership roles and do not consume the four Core Member scanner slots.

The backend must enforce this limit.

Do not rely on a disabled frontend button or a JavaScript count.

### Permission management

A Core Member may have:
- `can_scan_qr`
- Other explicitly authorized permissions, if required.

Only the President, Vice President or Super Admin, according to the configured policy, can grant or revoke Core Member permissions.

### Concurrency

Use a PostgreSQL transaction and a club-scoped locking strategy when granting scanner permissions.

Two simultaneous requests must never result in five active scanner-enabled Core Members.

Use an appropriate database constraint or transactional enforcement strategy.

Recheck permissions during every scanner operation.

