# SECTION 9 — UNIQUE QR CODE GENERATION

Each successful registration must receive an individual QR code.

### Token security

- Generate cryptographically secure random tokens.
- Store only a secure hash of the token.
- Associate the token with one registration.
- Do not place student email, registration number or internal database ID inside the QR payload.
- Do not expose the stored hash.
- Do not reuse QR tokens.
- Support revocation where a registration is cancelled.

The QR code should contain only an opaque verification token or secure verification payload.

Do not treat a frontend-generated QR code as proof of registration.

The backend is the authority.

