# SECTION 16 — SECURITY REVIEW

Perform a security review of every new workflow.

### Authentication

- Validate Supabase JWT signature.
- Validate issuer, audience, expiration and subject.
- Use appropriate signing-key verification.
- Do not accept arbitrary user identity headers.
- Do not trust client metadata for permissions.

### Authorization

- Enforce global and club-scoped roles on the backend.
- Prevent IDOR vulnerabilities.
- Prevent cross-club access.
- Prevent unauthorized leadership assignment.
- Prevent Core Member privilege escalation.
- Enforce scanner limits transactionally.
- Recheck permissions during every attendance scan.

### Invitation security

- Secure invitation lifecycle.
- Expiring invitations.
- Single-use acceptance.
- Revocation.
- No plaintext passwords.
- No exposed service-role credentials.

### Database

- RLS enabled and actual policies reviewed.
- Least-privilege runtime role.
- No BYPASSRLS.
- Safe transaction context.
- Safe SECURITY DEFINER functions.
- Appropriate unique constraints.
- No migration credentials used at runtime.

### QR security

- High-entropy tokens.
- Hash at rest.
- One registration per token.
- Atomic check-in.
- Unique attendance.
- Replay prevention.
- No personal data inside QR payload.

### Web application

- Secure CORS.
- Rate limiting.
- Request validation.
- Output encoding.
- CSRF protections where applicable.
- Safe error messages.
- Secure HTTP headers.
- Upload functionality must not be added unless explicitly required.

Do not claim security merely because Helmet or RLS is enabled.

Demonstrate actual authorization and concurrency tests.

